<http://data.silknow.org/object/7d0286d0-9492-3b5b-9ae4-a2bcb47f5be7/observation/3>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "This petite vest would have most likely been worn over a one-piece Manchu styled robe. The vest as an item of woman's clothing may have had its origins either in a woman's ceremonial vest known as the <i>xiapei</i>, or perhaps even the riding jacket known as the <i>gua</i>. \n\nThis vest is unique in its construction: usually, vests have only a sideways opening held by buttons, but in this case, the entire front panel is held to the shoulders and back-piece with buttons. The buttons have a white enamelled face decorated as a clock-face with Roman numerals: if these had not been a later alteration by the vest's subsequent European collectors, it may be an indication of a Western influence on Qing dynasty dress."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/7d0286d0-9492-3b5b-9ae4-a2bcb47f5be7> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/7d0286d0-9492-3b5b-9ae4-a2bcb47f5be7/dimension/4>
